{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775344882-CHExmc0XpgQWxOf7TZ9U","role":"assistant","created":1775344889,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This confirms the situation. Looking at the 1952-12 data (which has separate Air Force column starting from 1949), I can see that:\n\n1. In 1945-1947, there was no separate \"Air Force\" column - these were included in Army\n2. From 1949 onwards, the Air Force is separated out as its own column\n\nSo the 1948-04 document shows the correct data for the reporting structure where Air Force expenditures were still charged to Army appropriations (pre-1947, and the data is as of before Air Force became a separate department in 1947).\n\nFrom the 1948-04 Treasury Bulletin (page 13):\n- FY 1940: Department of the Army = 667 million dollars\n- FY 1947: Department of the Army = 7,425 million dollars\n\nThe increase = 7,425 - 667 = 6,758 million dollars\n\nLet me double-check: 7,425 - 667 = 6,758\n\nYes, that's correct.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_d5c19ea888b64d7a8c0e60ca","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/answer.txt","content":"6758"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
